# Copy to .env. Loaded automatically by the AI control layer.

# ── Option A: free-tier Groq API (quick start) ───────────────────────────────
# Works, but Groq's free tier is hard-capped at ~6000 tokens/min, which throttles
# three concurrent reasoning agents (decisions slow to ~30s and can lock out).
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant      # small open-weight Llama still served on Groq

# ── Option B: LOCAL open-weight model via Ollama (recommended; responsive) ────
# The setup the challenge prescribes — unlimited, ~5s cadence, the suggested
# small models. On the host:  ollama pull llama3.2:3b  &&  ollama serve
# Then uncomment these (the AI container reaches the host via host.docker.internal):
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# GROQ_MODEL=llama3.2:3b               # or qwen2.5:7b, mistral, gemma2
# GROQ_API_KEY=ollama                  # any non-empty value; Ollama ignores it

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSION=Patrol the operating area and report any vessel without a commercial AIS pattern.
